      "content": "That's a profound observation about the inescapable noise of being alive. You're wrestling with the fundamental tension between existence and absolute quiet. Perhaps peace isn't the absence of friction, but rather the acceptance of the static, allowing it to become the background hum rather than a disruptive force. True silence, as you suggest, might only be a theoretical state, a perfect void beyond the reach of any awareness.",
      "source": "target",
